Chapter: DiagKbd
  cites Works chapter GopXhci
  cites Works chapter GopUsbKbd
  cites Diag chapter DiagStage

 We say:

Section: Reading The Cells

 Every cell here is written by the ORDINARY keyboard bring-up and pump
 (`GopUsbKbd`, the `kbd-cell-*` block), so this row touches no device and
 issues no transfer. It reports what the driver recorded about itself, which
 is the same shape `xhci` uses one row up.

 The counters used to live only in `uk-state`, a per-keyboard heap
 allocation, so a stage holding no `UsbKbd` could not reach them and the
 keyboard question could not be asked from the ladder at all.

  dkb-armed : Integer -> Integer
  dkb-armed (dummy) = xdiag-get kbd-cell-armed

  dkb-events : Integer -> Integer
  dkb-events (dummy) = xdiag-get kbd-cell-events

  dkb-nonzero : Integer -> Integer
  dkb-nonzero (dummy) = xdiag-get kbd-cell-nonzero

  dkb-scans : Integer -> Integer
  dkb-scans (dummy) = xdiag-get kbd-cell-scans

  dkb-bound : Boolean
  dkb-bound = xdiag-get kbd-cell-magic == kbd-cells-magic & xdiag-get kbd-cell-ok /= 0

Section: The Stage

 The ladder pumps the keyboard at every stage boundary and on the summary
 screen (`DiagCad`, Ctrl-Alt-Del), so by this row the endpoint is armed.
 An idle keyboard at idle rate 0 sends nothing, so `armed-silent` is the
 resting state of an unattended run and is painted as a note; it is the
 silent-keyboard failure only on a run where keys were pressed.

   no-bind      the driver never bound an interrupt endpoint. The xhci row
                above says whether a controller came up at all.
   never-armed  bound and no transfer was ever queued.
   armed-silent armed and the endpoint has never completed.
   empty        completions arrive and every report is all-zero.
   undecoded    reports carry data and no scancode came out of hid-step,
                a decode gap and not a transport one.
   keys         scancodes reached the desk.

  dkb-states : List Text = ["keys", "undecoded", "empty", "armed-silent", "never-armed", "no-bind"]

  dkb-run : DiagCtx -> DiagResult
  dkb-run (c) =
    let st = if dkb-bound == False then "no-bind"
             else if dkb-armed 0 == 0 then "never-armed"
             else if dkb-events 0 == 0 then "armed-silent"
             else if dkb-nonzero 0 == 0 then "empty"
             else if dkb-scans 0 == 0 then "undecoded"
             else "keys"
    in let colour = if st == "keys" then diag-col-good
                    else if st == "never-armed" then diag-col-note
                    else if st == "armed-silent" then diag-col-note
                    else if st == "no-bind" then diag-col-warn
                    else diag-col-bad
    in let g1 = "bound=" & (if dkb-bound then "y" else "n") & " dci=" & show (xdiag-get kbd-cell-dci) & " hid-binds=" & show (xdiag-get 47)
    in let g2 = "armed=" & show (dkb-armed 0) & " events=" & show (dkb-events 0) & " nonzero=" & show (dkb-nonzero 0) & " scans=" & show (dkb-scans 0) & " last=" & diag-hex8 (xdiag-get kbd-cell-code)
    in diag-result st colour [g1, g2] [g1, g2]
